WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.132
Even without a plotting library, we can demonstrate the logic of a bar chart.

00:00:05.132 --> 00:00:09.097
The dictionary stores counts for web, email, and store.

00:00:09.097 --> 00:00:15.185
Repeating the block character creates a bar whose length matches the count.

00:00:15.922 --> 00:00:23.989
Web has the longest bar because it has twelve observations, followed by email with seven and store with four.

00:00:23.989 --> 00:00:29.194
The visual encoding is simple: larger values produce longer bars.
